{"id": "0c2c8e73-ef5d-46e7-be10-ff203b783ce0", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "This requires cross-referencing ECR lifecycle policies against images currently in use by running workloads (ECS/EKS/Lambda) across every repo — that's a lot of scanning and correlation, so let me look into it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_2GMMUri5z2GEHlIKwErQcA", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "For every ECR repository in AWS account 012345678901_1, region us-east-1: (1) fetch the repository's lifecycle policy (if any) and parse its rules (tagStatus, tagPrefixList/tagPatternList, countType, countNumber/countUnit/countBeforeSince, action). (2) List images in the repo with their tags, digests, and pushed-at dates. (3) Determine which images are currently in use by running workloads in this account/region — check ECS task definitions referenced by running/active ECS services and tasks, EKS pod specs (if any EKS clusters exist), and Lambda functions using container image package type. Resolve the exact image digest/tag each running workload references. (4) For each repo, simulate the lifecycle policy rules against the actual image list to determine which images WOULD be selected for expiration/deletion under current rules. (5) Cross-reference: flag any image that is both (a) currently referenced by a running workload and (b) matched by an expiration rule in that repo's lifecycle policy.",
  "context": "User wants a safety audit: are any ECR lifecycle policies set up in a way that would delete an image tag/digest that is actively running right now (in ECS, EKS, or Lambda)? This is a bounded cross-referencing/audit task, not a root-cause investigation.",
  "resources": ["all ECR repositories in account 012345678901_1, region us-east-1", "ECS clusters/services/tasks in us-east-1", "EKS clusters in us-east-1 (if any)", "Lambda functions with container image package type in us-east-1"],
  "timeframe": "current state as of now",
  "criteria": "For each repository, report: whether it has a lifecycle policy, a plain-English summary of its expiration rule(s), which images are currently running against it (source: ECS service/task def, EKS pod, or Lambda function name), and whether any currently-running image would be matched/deleted by the policy. Call out high-risk repos explicitly."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Survey ECR repos, lifecycle policies, and running workloads in us-east-1 to cross-check deletion risk."}], "created_at": null}
